  "description": "GENYUW crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H112 Br4 N8 Nd8 O70 Zn6,4(C1 H4 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4A (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn1A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2A (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn3A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 23 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.185-5.039 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.57-152.25°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd8Zn6(L1)2(OAc)20(O)2(NO3)4(OH)4] (crystal: C84H112Br4N8Nd8O70Zn6·4MeOH·3H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 20 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 20 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
